  "live_records": {
    "q-159628": {
      "dom_id": "step-q159628",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider a sample of size ${n}_{1}=54$ from a population with standard deviation ${\\sigma }_{1}=3.7$ and a sample of size ${n}_{2}=77$ from a population with standard deviation ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.2.$ Given that the samples are independent and the sample means are ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}=23$ and  ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}=12,$ find a $99%$ confidence interval for the difference ${\\mu }_{1}-{\\mu }_{2}$ between the corresponding population means.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z>2.576)=0.005,$ where $Z∼N(0,1).$*",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that\n\n- the samples are independent,\n\n- both sample sizes are \"sufficiently large,\" i.e., $\\ge 30,$ and\n\n- both population variances are known.\n\nAs a result, given a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the difference ${\\mu }_{1}-{\\mu }_{2}$ between the corresponding population means can be written as\n\n$$\n({\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}-{\\overset{―}{x}}_{2})\\pm E\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $E={z}_{\\alpha /2}\\sqrt{\\frac{{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}}{{n}_{1}}+\\frac{{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}}{{n}_{2}}}$ is the margin of error,\n\n- ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}$ and ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}$ are the sample means, ${\\mu }_{1}$ and ${\\mu }_{2}$ are the population means, ${\\sigma }_{1}^{2}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}^{2}$ are the population variances,  ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are the sample sizes,\n\n- $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nNow, to construct the confidence interval, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1.** Find the point estimate:\n\n$$\n{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}-{\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}=23-12=11\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the margin of error. Since we are interested in finding a $99%$ confidence interval, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.99=0.01\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.005.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(Z>2.576)=0.005.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{z}_{\\alpha /2}={z}_{0.005}=2.576.\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the margin of error:\n\n$$\nE=2.576\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{{3.7}^{2}}{54}+\\frac{{1.2}^{2}}{77}}≈1.344\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** Construct the $99%$ confidence interval for the difference between the population means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & 11\\pm 1.344\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
